{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1365275-another-way-to-use-the-jovian-or-someone-similar","id":1365275,"title":"Another Way to Use The Jovian,Or Someone Similar.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-04T09:19:21-08:00","id":1365275,"title":"Another Way to Use The Jovian,Or Someone Similar.","content":"The Jovian,perhaps the ultimate enemy of all Prometheans. An supposed Fallen Qashmall ready to stop the Pilgrimage of all of them. He's a brilliant story hook.<br /> He got me thinking,what else could be done with the idea of a Qashmall who has separated itself from The Principle?<br /> The Jovian is a really cool plot hook that can be done with this idea. Are there others?<br /> Now,bear with me here,what if the Jovian is one of a few of the Fallen? Once more,are there others? <br /> One might think once the Jovian is in the game,Alchemists might feel like weak antagonists. But what if an Alchemist manages to capture and imprison A Qashmall for his own uses? My basic idea,is that an Alchemist learns of the Jovian. And decides if this one could Fall,then others can. So somehow the Alchemist captures,binds and enslave an Qashmall who's otherwise loyal to the Principle? And uses his new slave an a weapon to his own,all too human all too flawed ends?<br /> Would you use that idea I your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T20:18:10-07:00","id":1390905,"title":"","content":"One thing that strikes me is that the Jovian's basic motivation is a more free-range version of the drives that lead Pandorans and insatiate alchemists to imprison the Created: it wants them to strive ceaselessly and fruitlessly, and it can't pen a character in like that if they reach the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> The problem this presents for alchemists is that it's a grander-scale confinement than they usually deal with, and &quot;try to make an angel of ineffable fire into an incarnate curse upon the things I make my potions from&quot; feels like a reach as far as bright ideas from the insatiate go; if one is to bridge the gap, I think it almost certainly needs to be a step upward from the alchemist rather than an attempt to pull the Jovian or its analog down to the level that Vitriol-hunters usually operate at.<br /> <br /> The best approach, I think, is to hit the middle ground of insidiousness by having the Jovian (&quot;real&quot; or artificial) collaborate with a guild of alchemists to cage one or more Prometheans in a broad area to pickpocket or extort their resources in the long term; the fact that the Jovian is immortal and knows every milestone most Prometheans have allows for a hefty degree of insight to be leveraged to the end of manipulating the board at the societal level and further entrapping the Created and their mortal pursuers in a neverending chain of extracted Vitriol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}